@startuml state_hub_health
!theme plain
title Hub Health State Machine

skinparam state {
    BackgroundColor<<healthy>> #E8FDE8
    BackgroundColor<<warning>> #FDFDE8
    BackgroundColor<<critical>> #FDE8E8
    BackgroundColor<<new>> #E8E8FD
}

[*] --> UNREGISTERED

state UNREGISTERED <<new>>
state ONLINE <<healthy>>
state DEGRADED <<warning>>
state OFFLINE <<critical>>

UNREGISTERED --> ONLINE : HubAnnounce received\n[registry.register()]

ONLINE --> DEGRADED : check_health()\n[elapsed > timeout/2]
ONLINE --> ONLINE : HubAnnounce received\n[update_heartbeat()]

DEGRADED --> ONLINE : HubAnnounce received\n[update_heartbeat()]
DEGRADED --> OFFLINE : check_health()\n[elapsed > timeout]

OFFLINE --> ONLINE : HubAnnounce received\n[register() with status recovery]
OFFLINE --> [*] : HubDeregister received\n[registry.deregister()]

ONLINE --> [*] : HubDeregister received\n[registry.deregister()]
DEGRADED --> [*] : HubDeregister received\n[registry.deregister()]

ONLINE : Heartbeat within timeout/2
ONLINE : Hub fully responsive
ONLINE : Status reports received

DEGRADED : Heartbeat missed (timeout/2 < elapsed < timeout)
DEGRADED : Hub may be experiencing issues
DEGRADED : Awaiting next heartbeat

OFFLINE : Heartbeat exceeded timeout
OFFLINE : HUB_OFFLINE broadcast sent
OFFLINE : Commands rejected (ValueError)

note right of ONLINE
  **Triggers:**
  - HubAnnounce (heartbeat)
  - HubStatusReport
  - update_heartbeat()

  **Timeout default: 30s**
  degraded threshold: 15s
  offline threshold: 30s
end note

note right of OFFLINE
  **On transition to OFFLINE:**
  1. orchestrator.tick() detects timeout
  2. Broadcasts HUB_OFFLINE event
  3. FleetClient triggers
     on_hub_offline callbacks
  4. send_command() rejects
     with ValueError
end note

note bottom of UNREGISTERED
  **Hub lifecycle:**
  Each hub starts unregistered.
  HubAgent.start() sends initial
  HubAnnounce to trigger discovery.
end note

@enduml
